# Building a counterfactual state: synthetic control and Proposition 99
subtitle: "How to build a California that never passed Proposition 99 from a weighted blend of other states, and how placebo runs say whether its 26-pack gap is real."
tags: ["synthetic control","proposition 99","tobacco tax","comparative case study","placebo inference"]
teaches: ["methods/synthetic-control","methods/placebo-inference","methods/difference-in-differences"]
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed","b":"gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; steady, lively pace, never slow"}
next: {"title":"Reading a null: power, precision, and the Oregon blood-sugar result","href":"https://drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/dcast/causal-inference-in-economics-evidence-from-health-and-health-care/reading-a-null-power-precision-and-the-oregon-blood-sugar-result.cast"}

