    card title "A blend of states"

If no single state moves like California, which states should stand in for it? Start with what must be matched (@highlight ca@): its nineteen years before the tax.
    draw axes tk100 tk200 tx1970 tx1988 ca ca_lab

The closest single state is Monta (@draw h1 h2 hrule r1a r1b@)na, and even Montana misses California by about four and a half packs a year.
    draw mt mt_lab

The plain avera (@draw avg avg_lab@)ge of all thirty-eight does fa (@draw r2a r2b ourcalc@)r worse: it misses by sixteen.
    erase mt mt_lab

    erase avg avg_lab

Now take two states that look nothing like California. Utah, where few people smoke: about sixty-five packs a head in 1970.
    draw ut ut_lab

And Nevada, where many do: about a hundred and ninety. Both curves are smoothed versions of the yearly figures.
    draw nv nv_lab

Neither comes close. But California runs between them, year after year.
    highlight ca

So mix them: give Nevada a weight, w, give Utah the rest, and average their sales year by year.
    draw f1

At w equal to zero the mix is simply U (@point at.data [1979,78] gesture underline@)tah, and it misses California by forty-five packs a year.
    draw blend r3a r3b

Grab the dashed mix and pull it up toward Nevada, and watch the miss in the table: find where it is smallest.
    explore params ["w"] watch "Watch the mix rise from Utah toward Nevada: the miss in the table falls, then grows again."

The miss bottoms out at w of about 0.43, where the mix misses by just over three packs.
    animate w 0.43 duration 5

Two states that resemble California in nothing but their smoking already beat the best single state, and beat the average by far.
    highlight r3a r3b

The weights obey two rules: none is below zero, and together they add up to one.
    highlight f1 effect underline

So the mix always lies between real states, somewhere in the band they span.
    point at.data [1979,140] gesture circle duration 3

Allow negative weights, and a formula could fit the past by reaching far beyond anything a real state did, and then guess wildly about the future.
    point at.data [1979,240] gesture underline duration 6

Abadie, Diamond and Hainmueller let a computer search all thirty-eight states und (@highlight f1 effect underline@)er those rules, and it picked five.
    erase blend ut nv ut_lab nv_lab

Utah a third, Nevada and Montana about a fifth each, Colorado a sixth, and Connecticut the small rest.
    morph f1 tex ".33\\,UT + .23\\,NV + .20\\,MT + .16\\,CO + .07\\,CT"

They chose it to match the price of cigarettes, income, the share aged fifteen to twenty-four, beer drinking a (@draw r4a r4b@)nd past sales, and its yearly sales miss California's by under two packs.
    draw syn

That is synthetic California: a state no one lives in, built only from the record before the tax.
    highlight ca syn

