      authors: Orzechowski and Walker
      year: 2005
      finding: 'Packs sold per person: California 123.0 (1970), 90.1 (1988), 41.6 (2000); average of the 38 donor states 120.1 (1970), 113.8 (1988). Figures for the blends, misses and placebo re-runs in this lecture are computed from these data.'
takeaways:
    - Build the stand-in from the past
    - Weights never negative, sum to one
    - Placebos say how rare the gap is

