  lines:
    female|a||Did California's 1989 tax on cigarettes make people smoke less, and if so, by how much?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7240
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||Here is the state''s own record: packs sold per person each year, about a hundred and twenty-three in 1970.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:2jgxsx'
    female|a||By 1988 that was down to ninety.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 3120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:kvbnjk'
    'female|a||That November, voters passed Proposition 99: twenty-five cents more tax on every pack from January 1989, with the money spent on anti-smoking campaigns and health education.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:4i1rdf'
    female|a||After it, sales kept falling, to about forty-two packs by 2000.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:n9uqkq'
    'female|a||The naive answer reads the effect straight off the line: forty-eight packs fewer, all of it thanks to the tax.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:cux97g'
    'female|a||But look to the left of the vote: sales had been falling for a decade before anyone cast a ballot.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:7xfxv'
    female|a||So part of those forty-eight packs would have gone anyway. The question is how many.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:i4ne7o'
    'female|a||What we need is California after 1988 without the tax: its untreated outcome, written Y of zero, year by year.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:rjny48'
    female|a||And with one treated state, that path is never observed, so something else has to stand in for it.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1acup1c'
    'female|a||The obvious stand-in is the other states: here, the average of thirty-eight that ran no large anti-smoking programme and raised no big tax in these years.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:dssdou'
    'female|a||In 1970 the two sit close: a hundred and twenty-three packs for California, a hundred and twenty for the average.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1nv5toi'
    female|a||But by 1988 they are twenty-four packs apart, because California's sales started falling earlier, and fell faster.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:42t256'
    female|a||A quick check. Suppose we used the 38-state average anyway, in a difference-in-differences. The effect it gives the tax would be…:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ubfefl'
    'female|a||Too big: California was already falling faster than the average before 1989, and the comparison hands that head start to the tax.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9960
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||So a fair stand-in has to do what the average cannot: move like California before 1989.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6840
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||And no single state tracks it closely either, which is why the method we need does not pick a state. It builds one.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:11rd4v0'
    'female|a||If no single state moves like California, which states should stand in for it? Start with what must be matched: its nineteen years before the tax.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10520
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||The closest single state is Montana, and even Montana misses California by about four and a half packs a year.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1prai39'
    'female|a||The plain average of all thirty-eight does far worse: it misses by sixteen.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:174ct9f'
    'female|a||Now take two states that look nothing like California. Utah, where few people smoke: about sixty-five packs a head in 1970.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:11mlco2'
    'female|a||And Nevada, where many do: about a hundred and ninety. Both curves are smoothed versions of the yearly figures.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:5dggws'
    female|a||Neither comes close. But California runs between them, year after year.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1duwvpr'
    'female|a||So mix them: give Nevada a weight, w, give Utah the rest, and average their sales year by year.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:tpaahn'
    female|a||At w equal to zero the mix is simply Utah, and it misses California by forty-five packs a year.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1d3zdc7'
    'female|a||Watch the mix rise from Utah toward Nevada: the miss in the table falls, then grows again.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:a6u4ds'
    female|a||The miss bottoms out at w of about 0.43, where the mix misses by just over three packs.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7200
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Two states that resemble California in nothing but their smoking already beat the best single state, and beat the average by far.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:194igkz'
    'female|a||The weights obey two rules: none is below zero, and together they add up to one.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:koerzm'
    female|a||So the mix always lies between real states, somewhere in the band they span.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ku8aa1'
    female|a||Allow negative weights, and a formula could fit the past by reaching far beyond anything a real state did, and then guess wildly about the future.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1d1clyv'
    female|a||Abadie, Diamond and Hainmueller let a computer search all thirty-eight states under those rules, and it picked five.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ua0syq'
    female|a||Utah a third, Nevada and Montana about a fifth each, Colorado a sixth, and Connecticut the small rest.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1h87t25'
    female|a||They chose it to match the price of cigarettes, income, the share aged fifteen to twenty-four, beer drinking and past sales, and its yearly sales miss California's by under two packs.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 14000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1s4s8kw'
    'female|a||That is synthetic California: a state no one lives in, built only from the record before the tax.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:18k5xsu'
    female|a||So what does synthetic California say the tax did? Here is the real California again, from 1970 to 2000.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8480
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||The five-state blend has been fitted to everything left of the vote. To its right, it plays the California that never passed the tax.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:peiiqu'
    female|a||Your guess first. Synthetic California matches the real one up to 1988. Draw where you think it goes by 2000.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:zh4bwg'
    female|a||The shaded band was the distance between your line and the blend. Without the tax, the blend says, sales would have kept sliding slowly, to about sixty-seven packs per person in 2000.:
